{
 "id": "222-19",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "Now, as your mentor, I want to emphasize that my role is to guide and support you.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns, no matter how big or small.",
  "We're also here to help you navigate any challenges you may face during your projects.",
  "So, feel free to tap into the collective expertise of the team whenever needed.",
  "We need to experiment, take calculated risks, and sometimes fail forward.",
  "Instead of seeing failure as something to avoid, we view it as an opportunity for growth and innovation.",
  "We can also set aside time for hackathons or innovation sprints, where we step away from our regular tasks to focus on creativity and experimentation.",
  "We need to actively share our own ideas, embrace feedback, and show that we're open to trying new things and learning from our mistakes.",
  "Always start your variable names with 'm_'.",
  "It's a small detail, but it helps with uniformity and makes our code base more readable.",
  "Also, I want you to start using annotations for your functions.",
  "They provide clarity and help other developers quickly understand the purpose and types used in the function.",
  "We all need a break now and then to stay sharp and creative.",
  "I want to emphasize the importance of including assert statements in your methods.",
  "They add a layer of robustness to your code and help catch errors early.",
  "So, from now on, please include them consistently.",
  "Going forward, I'd like you to start your variable names with 'wr_'.",
  "This is to maintain consistency and make our code more readable."
 ],
